    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Exceptions thrown during the test execution may be intercepted and handled accordingly before propagating further, so that certain actions like error logging or resource releasing may be defined in specialized "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Extensions"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". JUnit Jupiter offers API for "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Extensions"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " that wish to handle exceptions thrown during "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Test"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " methods via "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "TestExecutionExceptionHandler"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "attachment$api/org.junit.jupiter.api/org/junit/jupiter/api/extension/TestExecutionExceptionHandler.html"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and for those thrown during one of test lifecycle methods ("
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@BeforeAll"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@BeforeEach"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@AfterEach"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@AfterAll"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ") via "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "LifecycleMethodExecutionExceptionHandler"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "attachment$api/org.junit.jupiter.api/org/junit/jupiter/api/extension/LifecycleMethodExecutionExceptionHandler.html"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The following example shows an extension which will swallow all instances of "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "IOException"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " but rethrow any other type of exception."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "public class IgnoreIOExceptionExtension implements TestExecutionExceptionHandler {\n\n\t@Override\n\tpublic void handleTestExecutionException(ExtensionContext context, Throwable throwable)\n\t\t\tthrows Throwable {\n\n\t\tif (throwable instanceof IOException) {\n\t\t\treturn;\n\t\t}\n\t\tthrow throwable;\n\t}\n}"
          }
        ],
        "language": "java",
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "An exception handling extension that filters IOExceptions in test execution"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Another example shows how to record the state of an application under test exactly at the point of unexpected exception being thrown during setup and cleanup. Note that unlike relying on lifecycle callbacks, which may or may not be executed depending on the test status, this solution guarantees execution immediately after failing "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@BeforeAll"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@BeforeEach"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@AfterEach"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " or "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@AfterAll"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "class RecordStateOnErrorExtension implements LifecycleMethodExecutionExceptionHandler {\n\n\t@Override\n\tpublic void handleBeforeAllMethodExecutionException(ExtensionContext context, Throwable ex)\n\t\t\tthrows Throwable {\n\t\tmemoryDumpForFurtherInvestigation(\"Failure recorded during class setup\");\n\t\tthrow ex;\n\t}\n\n\t@Override\n\tpublic void handleBeforeEachMethodExecutionException(ExtensionContext context, Throwable ex)\n\t\t\tthrows Throwable {\n\t\tmemoryDumpForFurtherInvestigation(\"Failure recorded during test setup\");\n\t\tthrow ex;\n\t}\n\n\t@Override\n\tpublic void handleAfterEachMethodExecutionException(ExtensionContext context, Throwable ex)\n\t\t\tthrows Throwable {\n\t\tmemoryDumpForFurtherInvestigation(\"Failure recorded during test cleanup\");\n\t\tthrow ex;\n\t}\n\n\t@Override\n\tpublic void handleAfterAllMethodExecutionException(ExtensionContext context, Throwable ex)\n\t\t\tthrows Throwable {\n\t\tmemoryDumpForFurtherInvestigation(\"Failure recorded during class cleanup\");\n\t\tthrow ex;\n\t}\n}"
          }
        ],
        "language": "java",
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "An exception handling extension that records application state on error"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Multiple execution exception handlers may be invoked for the same lifecycle method in order of declaration. If one of the handlers swallows the handled exception, subsequent ones will not be executed, and no failure will be propagated to JUnit engine, as if the exception was never thrown. Handlers may also choose to rethrow the exception or throw a different one, potentially wrapping the original."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Extensions implementing "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "LifecycleMethodExecutionExceptionHandler"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "attachment$api/org.junit.jupiter.api/org/junit/jupiter/api/extension/LifecycleMethodExecutionExceptionHandler.html"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " that wish to handle exceptions thrown during "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@BeforeAll"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " or "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@AfterAll"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " need to be registered on a class level, while handlers for "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "BeforeEach"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "AfterEach"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " may be also registered for individual test methods."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "// Register handlers for @Test, @BeforeEach, @AfterEach as well as @BeforeAll and @AfterAll\n@ExtendWith(ThirdExecutedHandler.class)\nclass MultipleHandlersTestCase {\n\n\t// Register handlers for @Test, @BeforeEach, @AfterEach only\n\t@ExtendWith(SecondExecutedHandler.class)\n\t@ExtendWith(FirstExecutedHandler.class)\n\t@Test\n\tvoid testMethod() {\n\t}\n\n}"
          }
        ],
        "language": "java",
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Registering multiple exception handling extensions"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
